1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:04,333
Is this okay?

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:06,433
Huh?

3
00:00:08,333 --> 00:00:12,133
Doing what real couples do.

4
00:00:25,367 --> 00:00:26,800
Hinata.

5
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,667
I'm sorry.

6
00:01:24,067 --> 00:01:27,233
About just now... I just...

7
00:01:31,633 --> 00:01:33,167
I'm going to head home for today.

8
00:01:33,667 --> 00:01:35,033
I'm sorry.

9
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:37,700
Hinata.

10
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:02,767
Hey, Boss.

11
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:04,767
Sorry to bother you when you're busy.

12
00:02:04,867 --> 00:02:07,533
Do we have any spare ice buckets?

13
00:02:08,333 --> 00:02:10,067
You're asking me that?

14
00:02:10,167 --> 00:02:11,167
Huh?

15
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,800
What's wrong? In a bad mood?

16
00:02:13,567 --> 00:02:15,467
Yeah, I guess.

17
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:18,867
What... did he get
into a fight with Hinata?

18
00:02:18,967 --> 00:02:20,800
Keep it down, he'll hear you.

19
00:02:23,733 --> 00:02:24,400
I'm hanging up.

20
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,933
Ah, sorry, sorry.

21
00:02:26,033 --> 00:02:28,667
There's something I want to tell you, Boss.

22
00:02:29,100 --> 00:02:30,933
Actually, lately...

23
00:02:42,033 --> 00:02:43,767
Looks like it's working.

24
00:02:43,791 --> 00:02:44,858
(Your Sky Club)

25
00:02:44,882 --> 00:02:46,667
"The staff had a terrible attitude
and our food never came. When

26
00:02:46,692 --> 00:02:47,757
we complained, they gave us
attitude. Even one star is too much."

27
00:02:47,782 --> 00:02:50,755
"A staff member spilled a drink on me and didn't
even apologize properly. The service is awful."

28
00:02:57,533 --> 00:02:59,433
Should we do it like last time?

29
00:02:59,733 --> 00:03:00,967
No.

30
00:03:03,367 --> 00:03:05,167
Let's take it up a notch.

31
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:17,600
Is this okay?

32
00:03:18,567 --> 00:03:19,900
Huh?

33
00:03:21,733 --> 00:03:25,200
Doing what real couples do.

34
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:47,967
Is that from when you
helped film the assignment?

35
00:03:48,467 --> 00:03:49,833
Whoa!

36
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:52,200
You scared me!

37
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:54,067
Was it really that scary?

38
00:03:54,167 --> 00:03:55,467
Of course it was!

39
00:03:55,833 --> 00:03:57,533
Didn't I tell you not to just barge in?

40
00:03:57,833 --> 00:03:59,833
Sorry, sorry. Oof.

41
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,567
Let me ask you something.

42
00:04:04,067 --> 00:04:07,133
Sis, how did you end up dating
your current boyfriend?

43
00:04:08,267 --> 00:04:09,500
Huh?

44
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:11,467
Why the sudden question?

45
00:04:11,867 --> 00:04:14,833
Ah, no reason...

46
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:16,700
I was just a little curious.

47
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,633
Huh?

48
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:22,700
Don't tell me you actually fell for him?

49
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:24,267
No way!

50
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:25,533
I don't think so.

51
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:27,800
Weren't you just staring at that video?

52
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,700
I was only watching it to edit...

53
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:37,767
Is Sora all you can think about right now?

54
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:53,333
♪ My feelings go up and down every day ♪

55
00:04:53,433 --> 00:04:57,100
♪ Only time keeps slipping away ♪

56
00:04:57,200 --> 00:05:00,933
♪ This love has long surpassed friendship ♪

57
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:04,100
♪ This must be love ♪

58
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:07,333
♪ This is my love ♪

59
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:09,667
♪ On the campus slope ♪

60
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:14,900
♪ We used to be nameless strangers ♪

61
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,033
♪ People passing by ♪

62
00:05:17,133 --> 00:05:22,167
♪ All rushing toward different futures ♪

63
00:05:22,267 --> 00:05:26,000
♪ After meeting you that summer ♪

64
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:29,200
♪ Destiny began to turn ♪

65
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:34,933
♪ Just go for it, yet I'm
still questioning myself ♪

66
00:05:35,033 --> 00:05:35,600
♪ I can't say it out loud ♪

67
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:39,867
♪ If this is love, it's hard to say ♪

68
00:05:39,967 --> 00:05:43,567
♪ What kind of expression
will you show tomorrow? ♪

69
00:05:43,667 --> 00:05:48,767
♪ This love is more than just friends ♪

70
00:05:48,867 --> 00:05:50,833
♪ This is love ♪

71
00:05:52,267 --> 00:05:53,700
"Your Sky Hare nochi Koi."

72
00:06:00,200 --> 00:06:03,100
Look, the negative reviews
have suddenly spiked.

73
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:05,840
(Episode 6: "Our Feelings")
What do you think, Boss?

74
00:06:06,467 --> 00:06:08,333
Should we start by reviewing the menu?

75
00:06:08,433 --> 00:06:10,209
But nothing like this has
ever happened before.

76
00:06:10,233 --> 00:06:11,067
Isn't it weird for this to
happen all of a sudden?

77
00:06:11,167 --> 00:06:11,833
I know.

78
00:06:11,933 --> 00:06:14,700
Then let's start with what we can do.

79
00:06:19,267 --> 00:06:20,500
Makoto!

80
00:06:26,367 --> 00:06:27,133
Hurry up!

81
00:06:27,233 --> 00:06:28,500
Get your boss out here!

82
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,667
(Hinata: Can we talk for a bit?)

83
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:37,467
Excuse me, what seems to be the problem?

84
00:06:37,567 --> 00:06:39,900
What the hell do you
mean, what's the problem?

85
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,200
There's hair in my food!

86
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:43,976
I'm so sorry.
We'll get you a new one right away.

87
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:45,009
Get your boss out here right now!

88
00:06:45,033 --> 00:06:46,567
Hey...

89
00:06:46,667 --> 00:06:48,300
There are other customers here.

90
00:06:48,833 --> 00:06:50,167
How can I help you?

91
00:06:50,267 --> 00:06:50,967
Who are you?

92
00:06:51,067 --> 00:06:52,533
I'm the boss here.

93
00:06:52,933 --> 00:06:55,133
There's hair in my food!

94
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
I am truly sorry.

95
00:06:58,100 --> 00:06:59,300
This meal is on the house.

96
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,133
This isn't about the money!

97
00:07:01,867 --> 00:07:03,067
Hey.

98
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,333
Is this the kind of garbage
you usually serve your customers?

99
00:07:08,200 --> 00:07:09,867
What's your deal, huh?

100
00:07:10,733 --> 00:07:11,433
Ow!

101
00:07:11,533 --> 00:07:13,100
That hurts, let go!

102
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:19,467
How dare you lay a hand on a customer?

103
00:07:20,367 --> 00:07:22,133
You all saw that, right?

104
00:07:22,233 --> 00:07:25,900
The boss of this place
just assaulted a customer!

105
00:07:26,600 --> 00:07:29,067
Hey, what's with that look?

106
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:31,133
Oh my...

107
00:07:35,600 --> 00:07:36,967
What's all this commotion?

108
00:07:41,933 --> 00:07:42,967
What?

109
00:07:43,067 --> 00:07:45,600
That's no way to treat a customer.

110
00:07:46,633 --> 00:07:48,133
Man.

111
00:07:48,833 --> 00:07:51,467
Your hygiene standards are a joke.

112
00:07:51,567 --> 00:07:53,600
This place is a dump.

113
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,733
I feel sorry for anyone
working in a place like this.

114
00:08:01,833 --> 00:08:03,267
What did you just say?

115
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:06,400
Didn't you hear me?

116
00:08:07,067 --> 00:08:08,833
You set that guy up, didn't you?

117
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:10,567
Huh?

118
00:08:11,167 --> 00:08:12,533
You're trying to pin this on me?

119
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,667
Cut the crap.

120
00:08:15,767 --> 00:08:17,833
Haha...

121
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:22,733
Aren't you just reaping what you sowed?

122
00:08:23,567 --> 00:08:24,900
Boss?

123
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:33,833
I heard you fly off the handle
at the slightest provocation.

124
00:08:37,833 --> 00:08:39,233
Hit the nail on the head, didn't I?

125
00:08:49,233 --> 00:08:51,267
Finally showing your true colors.

126
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,767
Stop fighting.

127
00:09:26,267 --> 00:09:28,033
Take it outside.

128
00:09:30,667 --> 00:09:32,387
You're ruining the restaurant's reputation.

129
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:45,333
That's just the kind of guy he is.

130
00:09:46,467 --> 00:09:47,333
Hinata.

131
00:09:47,433 --> 00:09:48,833
Now do you understand?

132
00:10:03,533 --> 00:10:05,233
You saw what just happened.

133
00:10:07,033 --> 00:10:08,300
Yeah.

134
00:10:09,100 --> 00:10:10,767
He's right.

135
00:10:12,133 --> 00:10:13,333
Huh?

136
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,800
That's exactly the kind of guy I am.

137
00:10:17,767 --> 00:10:19,533
You'd better stay away from me.

138
00:10:27,700 --> 00:10:28,933
I'm going to head home then.

139
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,800
Okay, I'll walk you.

140
00:10:33,267 --> 00:10:34,500
No need.

141
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,067
It's fine.

142
00:10:36,633 --> 00:10:38,233
I can go back by myself.

143
00:11:24,033 --> 00:11:25,833
Are you trying to ruin the place?

144
00:11:28,367 --> 00:11:29,900
I couldn't control myself.

145
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:34,267
This is the place
your dad left you, isn't it?

146
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:37,333
Haven't you been fighting
tooth and nail to protect it?

147
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:45,167
Hinata has been watching how hard you work.

148
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,900
Because of that...

149
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,200
Don't let him down
over something like this.

150
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,133
(Letter to Oji)

151
00:12:24,233 --> 00:12:26,713
"Thank you for your feelings,
but I'm sorry, I can't date you."

152
00:12:33,367 --> 00:12:37,067
Um... are you okay?

153
00:12:39,900 --> 00:12:43,300
Yeah, just leave me alone.

154
00:12:44,267 --> 00:12:46,833
But it looks like it hurts.

155
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,267
Here, take this.

156
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:06,867
Use it.

157
00:13:10,167 --> 00:13:11,733
Thank you.

158
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:18,467
Ah.

159
00:13:18,667 --> 00:13:19,933
Wait!

160
00:13:45,067 --> 00:13:46,533
Oji Senpai.

161
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:52,700
I'm sorry.

162
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:55,533
I scared you yesterday, didn't I?

163
00:13:58,533 --> 00:13:59,833
Yeah...

164
00:14:00,633 --> 00:14:02,067
A little bit.

165
00:14:02,167 --> 00:14:06,067
You didn't expect him to
be that dangerous, did you?

166
00:14:10,733 --> 00:14:14,600
I... I like you.

167
00:14:16,933 --> 00:14:20,000
That's why I wanted to steal you
away from him no matter what.

168
00:14:24,233 --> 00:14:26,033
Don't be with him, be with me...

169
00:14:28,933 --> 00:14:30,333
Date me.

170
00:14:31,333 --> 00:14:33,667
But for me... nothing has changed.

171
00:14:36,367 --> 00:14:37,833
I...

172
00:14:40,133 --> 00:14:41,967
I like Sora Senpai.

173
00:14:53,567 --> 00:14:58,367
I don't have romantic
feelings for you, Oji Senpai.

174
00:15:01,300 --> 00:15:03,767
And I've never liked you in that way.

175
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,033
It's my fault for not making it clear.

176
00:15:10,667 --> 00:15:12,000
I'm sorry.

177
00:15:38,233 --> 00:15:42,433
You should really get that wound treated.

178
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:46,933
That's not the point, is it?

179
00:16:36,233 --> 00:16:37,567
Hmm?

180
00:16:37,867 --> 00:16:39,200
Making any progress?

181
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:41,867
Well...

182
00:16:43,333 --> 00:16:46,133
You've been spinning
your pen this whole time.

183
00:16:47,100 --> 00:16:49,333
Daon, you look like you're
really good at studying.

184
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:51,867
No way, I'm terrible at it.

185
00:16:51,967 --> 00:16:54,367
Come on, you totally
look like a good student.

186
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,060
Not really.

187
00:17:08,700 --> 00:17:11,933
I have times when I can't focus, too.

188
00:17:16,267 --> 00:17:17,700
Like when?

189
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,367
Right now.

190
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,733
Why can't you focus right now?

191
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:40,133
Because something's bothering me.

192
00:17:40,233 --> 00:17:41,467
Huh?

193
00:17:42,700 --> 00:17:44,000
Oh, you mean the pen?

194
00:17:44,100 --> 00:17:45,633
Because I keep spinning it.

195
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:48,100
Yeah.

196
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,267
It's pretty distracting.

197
00:17:49,367 --> 00:17:50,900
Wait, seriously?

198
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:53,700
My bad...

199
00:18:00,033 --> 00:18:01,333
Sorry.

200
00:18:01,433 --> 00:18:02,567
I'll keep it down.

201
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,567
Can I stay a little longer?

202
00:18:09,467 --> 00:18:11,333
Ah, it's nothing...

203
00:18:11,433 --> 00:18:13,067
I just feel more motivated.

204
00:18:16,033 --> 00:18:17,967
I mean, that's really bothering me.

205
00:18:23,033 --> 00:18:24,367
What did you say?

206
00:18:25,267 --> 00:18:26,533
Uh...

207
00:18:29,333 --> 00:18:32,233
What did you say... "Kujisudago"?

208
00:18:33,333 --> 00:18:34,567
Shut up.

209
00:18:34,967 --> 00:18:37,467
That definitely wasn't
Japanese just now, right?

210
00:18:38,033 --> 00:18:39,209
And you said something like "Shikuro~".

211
00:18:39,233 --> 00:18:40,567
A fake couple?

212
00:18:40,967 --> 00:18:42,500
Yeah, it's all fake.

213
00:18:42,900 --> 00:18:44,200
Oh~.

214
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:47,367
To hide from Oji Senpai?

215
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:50,100
Yeah.

216
00:18:50,200 --> 00:18:52,000
How is Riku so calm?

217
00:18:53,200 --> 00:18:54,400
Riku, what are you doing?

218
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:55,909
"What did that Korean phrase mean?"
"I'm not telling you."

219
00:18:55,933 --> 00:18:56,933
What are you doing?

220
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:00,367
Nothing, it was obvious anyway.

221
00:19:00,467 --> 00:19:01,333
You knew all along?

222
00:19:01,433 --> 00:19:03,833
So, what's the plan now?

223
00:19:03,933 --> 00:19:06,600
You don't need to hide from
Oji Senpai anymore anyway.

224
00:19:06,700 --> 00:19:08,180
Are you going to cancel the contract?

225
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:12,500
- Well...
- Wait, no?

226
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:18,300
The thing is... I think I've
actually fallen for Senpai.

227
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:19,267
- Maybe.
- Huh?

228
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:21,567
- Seriously?
- Seriously?

229
00:19:22,667 --> 00:19:23,300
Nice, nice.

230
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:24,700
Stop it.

231
00:19:25,667 --> 00:19:27,167
Aren't you going to confess?

232
00:19:27,267 --> 00:19:28,467
Yeah, exactly.

233
00:19:29,567 --> 00:19:32,267
Sora Senpai, I like you.

234
00:19:32,367 --> 00:19:33,867
Please go out with me.

235
00:19:33,967 --> 00:19:35,367
Something like that.

236
00:19:50,967 --> 00:19:52,467
Hello, Mom?

237
00:19:53,467 --> 00:19:54,767
Huh?

238
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,933
Riku, what's wrong?

239
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:03,067
I heard my dad suddenly collapsed.

240
00:20:03,267 --> 00:20:05,167
I'm heading over there with my brother now.

241
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:07,133
What?

242
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:09,233
Where are you going?

243
00:20:09,633 --> 00:20:10,800
Hong Kong.

244
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,867
My dad works there.

245
00:20:17,367 --> 00:20:19,033
I hope everything's okay.

246
00:20:27,093 --> 00:20:29,361
"At the airport. He seems to
have regained consciousness,

247
00:20:29,385 --> 00:20:30,826
but he still needs
someone with him for now."

248
00:20:34,533 --> 00:20:37,233
Looks like he won't be back for a while.

249
00:20:44,067 --> 00:20:45,767
This is just who I am.

250
00:20:47,733 --> 00:20:49,567
You're better off staying away from me.

251
00:20:55,267 --> 00:20:56,267
Sorry, I have to go.

252
00:21:04,633 --> 00:21:05,900
Good luck!

253
00:21:09,267 --> 00:21:10,467
Ah!

254
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:16,333
He's dating me now.

255
00:21:18,300 --> 00:21:21,233
Then let's be a fake couple from now on.

256
00:21:21,933 --> 00:21:23,433
I look forward to it, Hinata.

257
00:21:43,100 --> 00:21:44,767
This is just who I am.

258
00:21:50,900 --> 00:21:52,333
But even so...

259
00:21:53,233 --> 00:21:57,667
I still like Sora Senpai.

260
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:10,133
We're about to board the plane.

261
00:22:12,033 --> 00:22:13,400
What's wrong?

262
00:22:25,867 --> 00:22:28,600
Hey, are you sure about this?

263
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:44,000
Sorry, I'm hanging up.

264
00:22:48,967 --> 00:22:50,700
I'm heading out.

265
00:22:51,733 --> 00:22:53,500
Make sure you contact Hinata.

266
00:23:12,333 --> 00:23:14,733
(Calling Hinata)

267
00:24:38,267 --> 00:24:40,100
I don't want to keep quiet anymore.

268
00:24:41,300 --> 00:24:42,767
I've had enough.

269
00:24:49,600 --> 00:24:51,309
(Next Episode Preview)
Is there a student like that?

270
00:24:51,333 --> 00:24:52,509
Is he an international student?

271
00:24:52,533 --> 00:24:55,233
(Their "end" is approaching—)
Should we end this?

272
00:24:55,333 --> 00:24:56,700
Please don't come any closer!

273
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:59,100
Let's do as you say and end this.

274
00:25:04,467 --> 00:25:06,767
Bun Bun, hello YouTube.

275
00:25:07,667 --> 00:25:09,867
Bun Bun...

276
00:25:11,067 --> 00:25:13,433
Bun Bun... hello YouTube.

277
00:25:15,300 --> 00:25:16,667
Let's eat.

278
00:25:16,767 --> 00:25:17,400
Mmh.

